WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.450
Lanthanum is the first element in a series
called the ‘rare earths’. They

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:11.469
are not terribly rare but never-the-less they
are called rare earths and

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:16.730
they all have rather similar names so there
is quite an amusing little

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:21.180
rhyme, mnemonic, that people learn to remember
the names which at

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:26.650
the first two letters of each word tell you
this chemical symbol the

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:31.260
elements so this goes ‘Language Centres
Praise Ned’s Promise of Small

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:35.500
European Garden Tubs. Dinosaurs Hobble Erotically
Thrumming Yellow

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:40.750
Lutes’, which takes us from lanthanum all
the way to lutetium.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.330
Lanthanum is the largest of the lanthanides.
It’s a prototype for the

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:49.110
lanthanide series and because it is the largest
it is the most reactive. It’s

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:53.130
a strange metal in that you can actually cut
it with a knife. So it’s not

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.190
actually that hard.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:59.761
I haven’t worked much with lanthanum but
one of my students or a

00:00:59.761 --> 00:01:03.649
Russian visitor did some rather interesting
experiments with making a

00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:08.530
compound of lanthanum and copper, so-called
lanthanum cuprate, which

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:10.310
is quite an interesting catalyst.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:16.020
Lanthanum’s got quite a few technological
uses. It’s used in, of all things,

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:21.340
lighting in Hollywood studios. Lanthanum can
also be used in hydrogen

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.609
storage though obviously the hydrogen economy
is becoming a very

00:01:24.609 --> 00:01:29.480
important issue with the energy crisis and
so on and so forth; and it’s, in

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.729
certain circumstances, it’s very effective
as what we called a hydrogen

00:01:32.729 --> 00:01:37.100
sponge so it can suck up all of the hydrogen
and then hopefully you

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:42.189
could use it as a fuel source. But because
it’s quite heavy it might not be

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:45.119
actually that useful in the end, but it’s
good to know that it can do that.

